&lt;li&gt;Experience working with enterprise customers and managing complex technical escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, presentation, and stakeholder management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively across Sales, Support, Product, Engineering, and Professional Services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and analytical skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-first mindset with strong ownership and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business-level English communication skills, with the ability to engage effectively with customers and internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on technical troubleshooting skills, with the ability to investigate complex enterprise and cybersecurity issues rather than relying solely on team escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead from the front during critical customer incidents, including technical triage, root-cause analysis, and coordination of resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to coach engineers through practical technical problem-solving while maintaining accountability for customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cybersecurity products, enterprise security platforms, or critical infrastructure protection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SaaS/platform deployments and enterprise adoption programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with large enterprise customers in Singapore.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with technologies such as malware protection, file security, email security, data security, network security, cloud security, or endpoint security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing strategic accounts and executive-level customer relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within the first year, the Customer Experience Manager will establish a strong local customer experience organization in Singapore, build trusted relationships with key customers, improve onboarding and platform adoption, create an effective escalation management process, and establish a strong feedback loop between local customers and OPSWAT’s global Product and Engineering teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ultimate goal is simple: ensure every OPSWAT customer in Singapore realizes maximum value from the platform and views OPSWAT as a trusted security partner—not simply a technology vendor.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;OPSWAT is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to providing an environment where equal employment opportunities are extended to all employees and applicants, free of discrimination and harassment of any type. All employment decisions are based on individual qualifications, job requirements, and business needs without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other category protected by federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recruiting Agencies: we do not accept unsolicited resumes from third party agencies for any of our open positions. To submit resumes for our jobs, there must be a recruiting contract approved by our legal team and endorsed by both parties. We are currently not accepting additional 3rd party agencies at this time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OPSWAT&lt;/span&gt;, a global leader in IT, &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OT&lt;/span&gt;, and &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;ICS&lt;/span&gt; critical infrastructure cybersecurity, delivers an end-to-end platform that gives public and private sector organizations and enterprises the critical advantage needed to protect their complex networks, secure their devices, and ensure compliance. Over the last 20 years our commitment to innovative technology has earned the trust of more than 1,700 organizations, governments, and institutions globally, solidifying our role in protecting the world’s critical infrastructure and securing our way of life.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Data Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;you will own the data foundation the team runs on:&amp;nbsp;dataset pipelines, labeling workflows, and data quality. Model quality is bottlenecked by data quality; this role removes that bottleneck. &lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;We&#39;ve had a strong presence in Veszprém for over a decade, and we&#39;re now expanding into Budapest, this role is based in our newly opening &lt;strong&gt;Budapest office&lt;/strong&gt;, right at the start of that growth.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will Have the Opportunity to&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain dataset ingestion, cleaning, and versioning pipelines (training, validation, and held-out evaluation sets)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and operate labeling workflows, including quality control and inter-annotator agreement tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own dataset testing: coverage analysis, class balance, leakage detection, dataset documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage dataset versioning and lineage so every model release traces back to exact training data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with data science and product engineering teams on data-sharing boundaries and formats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years data engineering experience; strong Python and SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data versioning tools (DVC, LakeFS, or similar) and pipeline orchestration (Airflow, Dagster, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of ML-specific data concerns: train/test leakage, label noise, distribution shift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rigor in documentation and reproducibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You&#39;ll Love Working Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovative Environment&lt;/strong&gt;: Join a team at the forefront of cybersecurity innovation. At OPSWAT, you&#39;ll have the opportunity to work with cutting-edge technologies and contribute to solutions that shape the future of cybersecurity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative Culture&lt;/strong&gt;: We foster a culture of collaboration, where every team member&#39;s input is valued. You&#39;ll have the chance to work alongside talented individuals who are passionate about cybersecurity and dedicated to making a difference.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Growth&lt;/strong&gt;: At OPSWAT, we prioritize the growth and development of our team members. You&#39;ll have access to ongoing training and development opportunities to enhance your skills and advance your career in cybersecurity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Impactful Work&lt;/strong&gt;: Join a mission-driven company that is committed to securing the digital world. Your work at OPSWAT will have a meaningful impact on organizations worldwide, protecting critical data and assets from evolving cyber threats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fun and Dynamic Atmosphere&lt;/strong&gt;: We believe in fostering a fun and dynamic work environment. From team-building activities to social events, you&#39;ll have plenty of opportunities to connect with your colleagues and enjoy the journey together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;OPSWAT is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to providing an environment where equal employment opportunities are extended to all employees and applicants, free of discrimination and harassment of any type. All employment decisions are based on individual qualifications, job requirements, and business needs without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other category protected by federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recruiting Agencies: we do not accept unsolicited resumes from third party agencies for any of our open positions. To submit resumes for our jobs, there must be a recruiting contract approved by our legal team and endorsed by both parties. We are currently not accepting additional 3rd party agencies at this time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OPSWAT&lt;/span&gt;, a global leader in IT, &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OT&lt;/span&gt;, and &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;ICS&lt;/span&gt; critical infrastructure cybersecurity, delivers an end-to-end platform that gives public and private sector organizations and enterprises the critical advantage needed to protect their complex networks, secure their devices, and ensure compliance. Over the last 20 years our commitment to innovative technology has earned the trust of more than 1,700 organizations, governments, and institutions globally, solidifying our role in protecting the world’s critical infrastructure and securing our way of life.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At OPSWAT, we’re on a mission to protect the world’s most critical infrastructure. As a U.S.-based cybersecurity leader, we specialize in developing solutions for threat prevention and process creation for secure data transfer and safe device access. With our rapidly growing R&amp;amp;D presence in Hungary, we are expanding the team behind our MetaDefender Sandbox and Threat Intelligence Service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;The MetaDefender Sandbox and Threat Intelligence Service are components of an advanced malware analysis solution that detects and analyzes zero-day and evasive threats using a combination of dynamic analysis, AI, and machine learning. It helps customers across the globe, including governments, financial institutions, and critical infrastructure operators, identify malicious behavior that traditional antivirus engines often miss. We are looking for a driven and passionate DevOps Engineer to join our international team. You’ll collaborate with colleagues from Hungary, USA, Vietnam, Spain, and Georgia, and contribute to building scalable, cloud-enabled, and on-premise threat detection solutions that make a real difference in the cybersecurity landscape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Work in an engineering team to develop and operate the product&lt;br&gt;• Production deployments&lt;br&gt;• Cloud automation&lt;br&gt;• Monitoring and alerting&lt;br&gt;• Incident management and post-incident analysis&lt;br&gt;• Identify and troubleshoot platform issues&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Need from You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• 2-5 years hands-on Hyperscaler experience (AWS, Azure, GCP, IBM Cloud, etc.)&lt;br&gt;• Cloud automation (terraform / ansible / others)&lt;br&gt;• Experience with Containerization (K8s, Docker)&lt;br&gt;• Experience with Linux systems&lt;br&gt;• Experience with the following technologies: Python, Bash, JavaScript and Node.js&lt;br&gt;• Software delivery (git, TeamCity)&lt;br&gt;• Excellent troubleshooting skills and a commitment to document findings&lt;br&gt;• Bachelor or Master’s degrees in software engineering, Information Technology,&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Computer Sciences or Mathematics&lt;br&gt;• Good written and verbal English communication skills&lt;br&gt;• Experience in TCP/IP network stack is welcome&lt;br&gt;• Cybersecurity background or understanding in the field is appreciated&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love Working Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;• Stable, growing international company background with an exceptional customer group&lt;br&gt;• The newest technology environment&lt;br&gt;• Extra benefits – supported sport activities (kettlebell training and football), massage, language courses, equipped kitchen etc&lt;br&gt;• Attractive working environment – nice office full of accessories (fruits every day, coffee, breakfast, tea etc.)&lt;br&gt;• Regular team events and Happy Hour activities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
