&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;If you are looking for a role where your decisions matter, your leadership is visible, and your work protects what matters most, we would love to meet you.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;OPSWAT is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to providing an environment where equal employment opportunities are extended to all employees and applicants, free of discrimination and harassment of any type. All employment decisions are based on individual qualifications, job requirements, and business needs without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other category protected by federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recruiting Agencies: we do not accept unsolicited resumes from third party agencies for any of our open positions. To submit resumes for our jobs, there must be a recruiting contract approved by our legal team and endorsed by both parties. We are currently not accepting additional 3rd party agencies at this time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OPSWAT&lt;/span&gt;, a global leader in IT, &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OT&lt;/span&gt;, and &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;ICS&lt;/span&gt; critical infrastructure cybersecurity, delivers an end-to-end platform that gives public and private sector organizations and enterprises the critical advantage needed to protect their complex networks, secure their devices, and ensure compliance. Over the last 20 years our commitment to innovative technology has earned the trust of more than 1,700 organizations, governments, and institutions globally, solidifying our role in protecting the world’s critical infrastructure and securing our way of life.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;builder-operator hybrid&lt;/strong&gt;—a Director of Supply Chain who can architect and scale a mature supply chain capability from the ground up, while remaining deeply involved in day-to-day operations. This role is hands-on and based in our Tampa warehouse, with a strong emphasis on &lt;strong&gt;build quality, QA/QC&lt;/strong&gt;, and operational excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be responsible for designing and executing a supply chain strategy that supports OPSWAT’s hardware growth, ensuring every unit shipped meets our standards for quality, branding, and customer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build &amp;amp; Scale Supply Chain Capability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Architect and implement scalable supply chain processes, systems, and vendor networks to support OPSWAT’s hardware growth trajectory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-On QA/QC Oversight&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Lead quality assurance and control efforts in the Tampa warehouse, including hardware assembly, imaging, testing, and packaging. Ensure every unit meets functional, security, and branding standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Warehouse Execution &amp;amp; Fulfillment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Oversee daily operations in the Tampa warehouse, including inventory control, ERP data accuracy, and fulfillment workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partner with Product Management to align supply chain execution with product specs. Work with Creative and GTM teams to ensure packaging and branding elevate the customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor &amp;amp; Logistics Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Build and manage relationships with suppliers, carriers, and logistics partners. Ensure compliance with export regulations and hardware-specific controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Metrics &amp;amp; Continuous Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Define and track KPIs across procurement, fulfillment, and QA/QC. Drive continuous improvement initiatives to enhance efficiency and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Hire, mentor, and lead a high-performing team of supply chain and warehouse professionals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Need From You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Supply Chain Management, Business, Engineering, or related field; MBA preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in supply chain operations, preferably in hardware or technology sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of managing global logistics, procurement, and fulfillment operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must possess a strong understanding of global compliance requirements, with a particular focus on export regulations and hardware specific controls when distributing goods across international borders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of ERP systems (e.g., NetSuite), demand planning, and inventory control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and cross-functional collaboration skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a fast-paced, high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Supply Chain, Engineering, or related field; MBA preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in supply chain operations, with experience in &lt;strong&gt;building&lt;/strong&gt; capabilities—not just running them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of &lt;strong&gt;hardware QA/QC&lt;/strong&gt;, ERP systems (NetSuite), and global logistics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in &lt;strong&gt;hands-on warehouse operations&lt;/strong&gt;, including assembly, imaging, and testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong grasp of export compliance and international trade regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead cross-functional initiatives and drive operational excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with shifting priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;OPSWAT is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to providing an environment where equal employment opportunities are extended to all employees and applicants, free of discrimination and harassment of any type. All employment decisions are based on individual qualifications, job requirements, and business needs without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other category protected by federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recruiting Agencies: we do not accept unsolicited resumes from third party agencies for any of our open positions. To submit resumes for our jobs, there must be a recruiting contract approved by our legal team and endorsed by both parties. We are currently not accepting additional 3rd party agencies at this time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OPSWAT&lt;/span&gt;, a global leader in IT, &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OT&lt;/span&gt;, and &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;ICS&lt;/span&gt; critical infrastructure cybersecurity, delivers an end-to-end platform that gives public and private sector organizations and enterprises the critical advantage needed to protect their complex networks, secure their devices, and ensure compliance. Over the last 20 years our commitment to innovative technology has earned the trust of more than 1,700 organizations, governments, and institutions globally, solidifying our role in protecting the world’s critical infrastructure and securing our way of life.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;h3 mb-4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;OPSWAT is a global leader in critical infrastructure protection — trusted by governments, defense agencies, and enterprise organizations across the world. We build technology that keeps the world&#39;s most sensitive environments secure. Our Singapore office is a strategic hub for our APAC and global operations, and this role sits at the center of that growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building — not inheriting. This is a hands-on&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Director role&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;for a builder-operator who can architect a world-class supply chain capability from the ground up and run it with precision. You will own the full picture: strategy, QA/QC, warehouse execution, vendor relationships, compliance, and team development. If you thrive in environments where you create the playbook and then execute it, this is your role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re interested in working as a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Director of Supply Chain&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;at OPSWAT, please apply, and we will get in touch!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will Have the Opportunity to&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and Scale Supply Chain Capability&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and implement scalable supply chain processes, systems, and vendor networks to support OPSWAT&#39;s hardware growth trajectory across APAC and globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the operating model — from sourcing through delivery — and build the infrastructure to sustain it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-On QA/QC Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead quality assurance and control across hardware assembly, imaging, testing, and packaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure every unit shipped meets OPSWAT&#39;s functional, security, and branding standards — no exceptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Warehouse Execution and Fulfillment&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee daily warehouse operations: inventory control, ERP data accuracy, and end-to-end fulfillment workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive operational discipline in a fast-paced, high-volume environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Management to align supply chain execution with product specifications and launch timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside Creative and GTM teams to ensure packaging and branding deliver a premium customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor and Logistics Management&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage strategic relationships with suppliers, carriers, and logistics partners across APAC and internationally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure full compliance with APAC and international export regulations and hardware-specific controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shipping and Customs Management&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage end-to-end shipping operations — domestic and cross-border — ensuring on-time delivery at optimal cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate customs processes, import/export documentation, and trade compliance requirements across multiple jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with freight forwarders and customs brokers to resolve issues proactively and keep shipments moving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Metrics and Continuous Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track KPIs across procurement, fulfillment, and QA/QC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Launch continuous improvement initiatives that raise quality standards and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, mentor, and lead a high-performing team of supply chain and warehouse professionals based in Singapore.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a team culture rooted in ownership, precision, and pride in work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Supply Chain Management, Engineering, Business, or a related field; MBA preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of supply chain operations experience, ideally in hardware or technology — with a track record of building capabilities, not just running them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with global logistics, procurement, and fulfillment operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with ERP systems, particularly NetSuite, demand planning, and inventory control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on knowledge of hardware QA/QC — assembly, imaging, testing, and packaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of APAC export regulations, international trade compliance, and hardware-specific controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English required; other language skills are an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable leading through ambiguity in a high-growth, fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;h3 mb-4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You&#39;ll Love Working Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic impact: You will build something that matters — a supply chain capability that directly enables OPSWAT&#39;s global hardware mission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global reach: Work closely with teams across North America, Europe, and Asia-Pacific.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership culture: At OPSWAT, we trust our people to lead. You will have the autonomy to build, decide, and execute.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mission-driven work: Our technology protects critical infrastructure worldwide. The work has real stakes — and real meaning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation, comprehensive benefits package, and professional development support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;OPSWAT is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to providing an environment where equal employment opportunities are extended to all employees and applicants, free of discrimination and harassment of any type. All employment decisions are based on individual qualifications, job requirements, and business needs without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other category protected by federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recruiting Agencies: we do not accept unsolicited resumes from third party agencies for any of our open positions. To submit resumes for our jobs, there must be a recruiting contract approved by our legal team and endorsed by both parties. We are currently not accepting additional 3rd party agencies at this time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OPSWAT&lt;/span&gt;, a global leader in IT, &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OT&lt;/span&gt;, and &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;ICS&lt;/span&gt; critical infrastructure cybersecurity, delivers an end-to-end platform that gives public and private sector organizations and enterprises the critical advantage needed to protect their complex networks, secure their devices, and ensure compliance. Over the last 20 years our commitment to innovative technology has earned the trust of more than 1,700 organizations, governments, and institutions globally, solidifying our role in protecting the world’s critical infrastructure and securing our way of life.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Position:&amp;nbsp;Director, Sales Finance&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a strategic &lt;strong&gt;Director, Sales Finance and Strategy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;to partner directly with our&amp;nbsp;go-to-market leadership,&amp;nbsp;CFO&amp;nbsp;and CEO.&amp;nbsp;As a direct report to&amp;nbsp;Head of FP&amp;amp;A,&amp;nbsp;you’ll&amp;nbsp;have a seat at the table and the opportunity to shape OPSWAT’s next phase of growth, including&amp;nbsp;public company&amp;nbsp;readiness.&amp;nbsp;This is a high-impact role responsible for&amp;nbsp;providing&amp;nbsp;the financial&amp;nbsp;insights, planning, and operational support needed to drive profitable revenue growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead all aspects of financial planning and analysis for the&amp;nbsp;go-to-market&amp;nbsp;organization, including&amp;nbsp;top-line (bookings,&amp;nbsp;billing,&amp;nbsp;ARR&amp;nbsp;and revenue),&amp;nbsp;operating expense management, sales compensation design and execution,&amp;nbsp;headcount planning,&amp;nbsp;and capacity and productivity models. The ideal candidate is a data-driven, strategic thinker with a proven ability to influence senior leaders and translate complex financial information into actionable business insights&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why This Role Matters&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are&amp;nbsp;expanding the capabilities of our&amp;nbsp;finance organization&amp;nbsp;to deliver faster, sharper, and more action-oriented insights that drive growth and capital efficiency. As a Finance Director, you will be the senior leader who will&amp;nbsp;be responsible for&amp;nbsp;transforming our&amp;nbsp;forecast&amp;nbsp;and planning&amp;nbsp;framework,&amp;nbsp;aligning&amp;nbsp;related&amp;nbsp;end-to-end processes, shaping&amp;nbsp;go-to-market&amp;nbsp;decision-making, and&amp;nbsp;championing&amp;nbsp;high quality profitable growth.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Planning and Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive&amp;nbsp;topline (billing,&amp;nbsp;revenue, ARR, etc.)&amp;nbsp;annual&amp;nbsp;operating&amp;nbsp;planning process,&amp;nbsp;quarterly&amp;nbsp;forecasts, and long-range scenarios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage all headcount planning, providing models and recommendations to support hiring plans and organizational structure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the management and forecasting of all departmental operating expenses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and present monthly and quarterly financial reporting packages for&amp;nbsp;go-to-market&amp;nbsp;leadership, including detailed variance analysis and commentary on business drivers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify&amp;nbsp;and communicate financial risks and opportunities to&amp;nbsp;t&amp;nbsp;he&amp;nbsp;business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales Leadership&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;HR&amp;nbsp;to design, model, and implement annual sales compensation plans that align with corporate revenue goals and strategic&amp;nbsp;objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the end-to-end administration of sales commissions, including quota and territory assignment validation, calculations, and ensuring&amp;nbsp;timely&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;accurate&amp;nbsp;payouts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the finance lead for the commission management&amp;nbsp;system&amp;nbsp;data integrity and process efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide detailed analysis on the effectiveness of compensation plans, SPIFFs, and other incentive programs, measuring ROI and performance against targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary point of contact for resolving commission-related inquiries and disputes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go-to-market Strategy&amp;nbsp;and Analytics:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop,&amp;nbsp;maintain, and enhance sophisticated sales capacity models to inform hiring targets, quota setting, and long-term revenue projections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze key metrics and SaaS KPIs, such as Customer Acquisition Cost (CAC), quota attainment, pipeline velocity, and sales cycle length.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide financial modeling and due diligence for strategic initiatives, including pricing strategies,&amp;nbsp;capital allocation,&amp;nbsp;new market entry, and partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with the&amp;nbsp;Sales&amp;nbsp;Operations&amp;nbsp;and IT&amp;nbsp;team to ensure alignment on data, systems, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Partnering and Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary financial advisor and trusted business partner to the&amp;nbsp;go-to-market&amp;nbsp;leadership team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively communicate financial performance and insights to executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and develop a&amp;nbsp;small&amp;nbsp;high-performing team of finance professionals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement and scalability in financial processes and reporting to support a growing sales organization.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Need from You&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;9+ years of progressively increasing responsibility in FP&amp;amp;A, Strategic Finance, or Corporate Finance leadership roles, ideally within SaaS/subscription and/or cybersecurity environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence and ability to communicate complex financial insights clearly to senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of SaaS metrics (TCV,&amp;nbsp;ARR, NRR, CAC,&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;pipeline to&amp;nbsp;billings) and&amp;nbsp;fluent in bookings-billings-revenue mechanics and revenue recognition guardrails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success partnering with&amp;nbsp;go-to-market&amp;nbsp;department heads to influence strategic decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;operating driver-based models,&amp;nbsp;achieving forecast accuracy, improving efficiency, and driving accountability through data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in finance, Accounting, Economics, or STEM field; MBA and/or CPA preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a market-based pay structure that varies by location.&amp;nbsp;The base pay for this position is dependent on location, as outlined below, as well as the candidate&#39;s knowledge, skills, and experience.&amp;nbsp;In addition to base pay, this role is eligible for bonuses, benefits, and equity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Pay Range: San Francisco Bay Area $220,000.00 - $260,000.00 &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
