&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OPSWAT&lt;/span&gt;, a global leader in IT, &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OT&lt;/span&gt;, and &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;ICS&lt;/span&gt; critical infrastructure cybersecurity, delivers an end-to-end platform that gives public and private sector organizations and enterprises the critical advantage needed to protect their complex networks, secure their devices, and ensure compliance. Over the last 20 years our commitment to innovative technology has earned the trust of more than 1,700 organizations, governments, and institutions globally, solidifying our role in protecting the world’s critical infrastructure and securing our way of life.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you purpose-driven? We are. At OPSWAT, our purpose is to secure the way of life we all enjoy. We focus our innovations on protecting the most critical infrastructure there is, such as manufacturing, nuclear facilities, financial institutions, governments, utilities, and more. You&#39;ve probably done some interesting things in your career, but how often can you say you&#39;ve contributed directly to the benefit of our global community with such a positive impact?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;“Critical Infrastructure” refers to a wide variety of systems, including not only traditional on-premise and cloud-based IT systems, but can also include operational technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Solution Engineer, you&#39;ll work alongside a peer group of talented professionals, splitting your time between the field and our lab team. Your job will be to uncover customer challenges, demonstrate how OPSWAT solves them, and guide customers through operationalizing the solution. You&#39;ll travel to customer sites and trade shows, collaborate with our CIP lab on demo kits and reusable demonstrations, and support RFPs alongside senior field SEs. You&#39;ll be required to maintain proficiency in the domains we serve, expertise in the products, and the disposition that makes a customer want to enthusiastically partner with you for their success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with AEs and partners to grow OPSWAT business through customer demos, proof of concepts, and technical evaluations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to customer sites and trade shows to present and support OPSWAT solutions, including working show booths&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the CIP lab team to build, maintain, and refine reusable demonstrations and mobile show lab kits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage customer requirements, expectations, and solution buy-in&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver detailed responses to RFPs in partnership with field and lab SEs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support proof of concepts, evaluations, and post-sale transitions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide pre-sales support to the OPSWAT Channel sales team to drive business and product proficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Need from You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience in cybersecurity or networking, with some customer-facing or pre-sales exposure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort presenting and leading discussions with customers, including technical and business stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize and meet deadlines while traveling and managing multiple engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Results-driven with an entrepreneurial mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence others to achieve results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal abilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptable, self-motivated, and open-minded&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience installing and troubleshooting enterprise applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-solving abilities; skilled at identifying and resolving technical issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It Would Be Nice if You Had&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in enterprise software or networking solutions, ideally within the network or device security space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Sandbox and anti-malware products and market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A technical understanding of APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with virtualized and cloud hosted environments (AWS, Azure, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with CRM software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
