&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OPSWAT&lt;/span&gt;, a global leader in IT, &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OT&lt;/span&gt;, and &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;ICS&lt;/span&gt; critical infrastructure cybersecurity, delivers an end-to-end platform that gives public and private sector organizations and enterprises the critical advantage needed to protect their complex networks, secure their devices, and ensure compliance. Over the last 20 years our commitment to innovative technology has earned the trust of more than 1,700 organizations, governments, and institutions globally, solidifying our role in protecting the world’s critical infrastructure and securing our way of life.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We are looking for a hands-on &lt;strong&gt;Senior Agentic Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to work closely with OPSWAT’s international Legal team and help accelerate and expand Legal’s use of AI and automation workflow. This role is part of the Enterprise Applications team and will operate as the dedicated Senior Agentic Software Engineering partner for Legal. The engineer will work day to day with Legal, join Legal team meetings, follow Legal’s priorities and roadmap, and translate Legal’s business, compliance, confidentiality, and governance requirements into practical technical solutions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The role will focus on building production AI applications, intelligent automations, agentic workflows, integrations, and analytics that improve how Legal operates across contracts, compliance, privacy, corporate governance, employment, regulatory monitoring, intake, knowledge management, and legal operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;What You Will Be Doing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Build, support, and integrate Legal AI and automation solutions across Legal’s core tools and platforms, including Chamelio for contract lifecycle management, Microsoft 365 Copilot, Claude, OneTrust, OPSWAT’s internally built Legal Service Desk and Entity Management system, and related enterprise applications, data platforms, document repositories, systems of record, and approved data sources.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Design and build new AI-powered legal applications, internal copilots, intelligent automations, agentic workflows, and API-based integrations that improve speed, consistency, visibility, quality, and control.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Serve as the technical translator for Legal: explain architecture, system limitations, access controls, data flows, integrations, model behavior, implementation trade-offs, and risk implications in plain language so Legal can make informed compliance and governance decisions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Partner with Legal stakeholders to identify high business impact use cases, understand workflows, define requirements, prioritize the engineering backlog, and deliver solutions that Legal can adopt and use in practice.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Manage Legal AI solutions end to end, from discovery, architecture, development, testing, deployment, monitoring, documentation, user training, support, adoption measurement, and continuous improvement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Help protect privileged, confidential, personal, employee, and sensitive business data through secure-by-design architecture, appropriate access controls, audit logging, retention alignment, and privacy-by-design practices.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Develop and operate evaluation, testing, and quality frameworks for Legal AI outputs, including accuracy, reliability, defensibility, source grounding, human review, and escalation to Legal where judgment is required.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Partner closely with Enterprise Applications, IT, Data, Security, and Legal to ensure Legal AI solutions align with enterprise architecture, security standards, governance requirements, and Legal’s operating model.&lt;/span&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;What We Need From You&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;5+ years of hands-on experience in software, data, automation, integration, platform, or applied AI engineering.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:714,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:150,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:357}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Production engineering: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Five or more years building and operating production software, with a track record of taking solutions from prototype to supported production.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:80,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Languages and fundamentals: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Python required; TypeScript or C# a plus. Tested, maintainable services; APIs; relational and document data stores; CI/CD; containers at a working level.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:80,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Applied agentic AI: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Successfully built and deployed production applications on LLM APIs that use retrieval-augmented generation, tool calling and multi-step agent workflows with human-in-the-loop controls and structured outputs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:80,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Evaluation discipline: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;You have built evaluation sets and quality metrics for LLM outputs and used them to gate releases.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:80,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Document processing: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Experience building document-processing pipelines that parse, OCR, extract, classify, and structure information from contracts, policies, corporate records, and other unstructured documents at realistic enterprise scale.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:80,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Security fundamentals: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Authentication and authorization, secrets management, encryption, audit logging and privacy by design, applied in systems that handled sensitive data.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:80,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;AI-assisted development: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Experience using agentic coding tools as a core part of how you build, and can show production work delivered faster because of it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Working with a non-technical function: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Ability to work effectively with non-technical legal function, understand legal and compliance workflows, explain technical concepts clearly, challenge assumptions where needed, and convert legal priorities into practical engineering solutions .&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:80,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Language: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Fluent English, written and spoken. Vietnamese is an advantage.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:80,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Education&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:150,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Data Science, Information Systems, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:714,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:150,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:357}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Relevant cloud, security, data, or AI engineering certifications are an advantage.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:714,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:150,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:357}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You&#39;ll Love Working Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meaningful work with passionate colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International working environment in global leading Cybersecurity product company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attractive compensation, regular assessments, and salary reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;13-month bonus &amp;amp; performance bonus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% salary, full insurances on probationary period.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extra-health care program (PVI) for employees and family members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ paid day off per year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attractive benefits for team activities (team building, team outing, sport, trade union activities).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice open office on the top of a building in District 3 full of accessories for active recreation, sport, fruits, coffee, and tea.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;OPSWAT is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to providing an environment where equal employment opportunities are extended to all employees and applicants, free of discrimination and harassment of any type. All employment decisions are based on individual qualifications, job requirements, and business needs without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other category protected by federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recruiting Agencies: we do not accept unsolicited resumes from third party agencies for any of our open positions. To submit resumes for our jobs, there must be a recruiting contract approved by our legal team and endorsed by both parties. We are currently not accepting additional 3rd party agencies at this time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OPSWAT&lt;/span&gt;, a global leader in IT, &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OT&lt;/span&gt;, and &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;ICS&lt;/span&gt; critical infrastructure cybersecurity, delivers an end-to-end platform that gives public and private sector organizations and enterprises the critical advantage needed to protect their complex networks, secure their devices, and ensure compliance. Over the last 20 years our commitment to innovative technology has earned the trust of more than 1,700 organizations, governments, and institutions globally, solidifying our role in protecting the world’s critical infrastructure and securing our way of life.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an innovative engineer for the GTM Product Team to strengthen the technology beneath OPSWAT&#39;s marketing operations. Marketing runs on HubSpot today, and it works hard for us: 1.1 million contacts, 817 active workflows, and the integrations that connect it to SugarCRM, Salesloft, My OPSWAT, websites and our data master. Your first job is to make that foundation more reliable — keeping the integrations healthy, resolving the sync and data-quality issues that slow the team down, and giving Marketing Operations a technical partner who understands their platform from the inside.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From there, you will help us build the next generation of that capability in house. The four functions HubSpot performs for us are the roadmap: marketing automation and email; lead capture from web, portal, events and webinars; lead management, meaning scoring, lifecycle and routing; contact data governance and consent and tight integration with our OPSWAT Data Master (ODM). Along the way you will bring AI into the product to enable smarter lead qualification, routing and scoring and more automated campaign managements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the Platform&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build one governed front door for every lead, whatever the source — web forms, My OPSWAT, webinars, field events, partner and list imports — so each lead is validated, de-duplicated, consented and enriched once, at the gate, and nothing reaches the CRM or the data spine any other way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build AI-native lead qualification: a model that reads fit and engagement across every signal we hold — product usage in My OPSWAT, Academy progress, web behavior, intent, firmographics — ranks the whole database with real resolution, explains every score in plain language, and learns from what SDRs actually convert.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build intelligent lead routing: the right lead to the right rep at the right moment, with territory, capacity, availability and priority held as data that Marketing Operations can shape and preview themselves, and a decision record behind every assignment so anyone can see why a lead went where it did.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make every hand-off dependable: each lead tracked from capture to first touch, stalls surfaced automatically, every priority tier followed up, and nothing lost between systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give Marketing Operations a self-service campaign layer: per-campaign behavior — routing, priority, nurture — configured in minutes with a preview of what it would have done to yesterday&#39;s leads, so new campaigns stop requiring new workflows and old overrides expire on their own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the platform AI-native from day one: expose its data and actions through an MCP server so OPSWAT&#39;s internal agents and assistants can look up a lead, explain a routing decision, or trigger a campaign action in natural language — and design every capability so an agent can use it as readily as a person can.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make consent and suppression a single source of truth, enforced at the gate and impossible to bypass, and stream every signal and every decision into OPSWAT Data Master so marketing, product and sales data finally join in one place.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the seams to SugarCRM, the email service provider, visitor identification, enrichment and My OPSWAT so that a failure in any one of them is contained, retried and visible — never silent, never lossy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leveraging OPSWAT Agentic SDLC — use the Platform team&#39;s agentic coding platform as your primary means of production, own the quality and security of what ships, and document the system as you go so it stays knowable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep HubSpot Running Through the Transition&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the health of HubSpot&#39;s existing integrations until each one is retired: the SugarCRM sync through the Sugar Data Tool, Salesloft, the My OPSWAT feed (portal and Academy), 6sense enrichment, web forms and the Forms API.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage and resolve integration incidents across HubSpot and its neighbors — root-cause them, fix them permanently, and write down what happened.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make safe, minimal changes in HubSpot when the business needs them, and hold the line against new workflow and list sediment that the migration would only have to unwind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the Forms Gateway pull-forward so website capture decouples from HubSpot early, and run the interim enrollment connector that keeps Salesloft working through cutover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile HubSpot and platform data continuously during the parallel run so drift is caught long before a cutover gate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Need From You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years building and operating production backend systems, with at least 3 in Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated, recent, daily practice building software with AI coding agents (Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot agent mode, Codex or similar). You can show us the workflow, the review and test loop, and something real that shipped through it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production support of a marketing automation platform&#39;s integrations — HubSpot strongly preferred; Marketo or Pardot considered — including its APIs, its data model, and its sync to a CRM. You have kept one of these healthy while other things changed around it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production experience with event-driven and durable-execution patterns: message queues, outboxes, idempotency keys, replay. Temporal or a comparable workflow engine strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on integration engineering against real vendor APIs — REST, webhooks, OAuth 2.0, rate limits, retries — built and operated, not configured through a wizard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PostgreSQL to a strong level: schema design, JSONB, partitioning, migrations with Alembic, and query performance work you can describe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud deployment on Azure or AWS: containers, infrastructure as code (Terraform or Bicep), CI/CD with GitHub Actions, secrets management, observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping LLM features into a product: structured outputs, evaluation discipline, confidence thresholds, fallbacks and guardrails — consuming a provided model gateway rather than building the infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and spoken English, and the skill to explain a technical trade-off to a marketing operations lead in their terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It Would Be Nice If You Had&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SugarCRM logic hooks and REST API, or another CRM&#39;s server-side extension model; Salesforce Apex or triggers transferable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Marketing technology domain knowledge: lead scoring and routing, consent and suppression, deliverability and ESP warm-up, campaign attribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;OPSWAT is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to providing an environment where equal employment opportunities are extended to all employees and applicants, free of discrimination and harassment of any type. All employment decisions are based on individual qualifications, job requirements, and business needs without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other category protected by federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recruiting Agencies: we do not accept unsolicited resumes from third party agencies for any of our open positions. To submit resumes for our jobs, there must be a recruiting contract approved by our legal team and endorsed by both parties. We are currently not accepting additional 3rd party agencies at this time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OPSWAT&lt;/span&gt;, a global leader in IT, &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;OT&lt;/span&gt;, and &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;ICS&lt;/span&gt; critical infrastructure cybersecurity, delivers an end-to-end platform that gives public and private sector organizations and enterprises the critical advantage needed to protect their complex networks, secure their devices, and ensure compliance. Over the last 20 years our commitment to innovative technology has earned the trust of more than 1,700 organizations, governments, and institutions globally, solidifying our role in protecting the world’s critical infrastructure and securing our way of life.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&quot;the-position&quot; data-line=&quot;11&quot;&gt;The Position&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-line=&quot;13&quot;&gt;We are looking for a hands-on engineer for the GTM Product Team to build&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;previewStrong_6bbb1f98&quot;&gt;Quantum&lt;/strong&gt;, OPSWAT&#39;s go-to-market platform. Quantum is where Sales, Sales Operations, Deal Desk, Order Operations, Marketing, Finance and leadership do their daily work: forecasting and pipeline, deal management, account research, quote-to-order review, territories and quotas, and data hygiene. It connects to DealHub CPQ, NetSuite, the OPSWAT Data Master (ODM), ZoomInfo, BambooHR and OPSWAT&#39;s AI platform, and it is in production today.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-line=&quot;15&quot;&gt;Quantum serves the whole go-to-market organization; this role focuses on its Sales capabilities. Its one big mission: make Quantum&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;previewStrong_6bbb1f98&quot;&gt;OPSWAT&#39;s CRM&lt;/strong&gt;, the system of record for accounts, contacts, leads, opportunities and activities, where every customer relationship begins and lives. Alongside that, you will keep shipping what the sales organization needs, keep Quantum&#39;s integrations healthy, be the technical partner Sales Operations can bring a problem to, and bring AI into every step of the deal: research, qualification, deal health, forecasting and order review.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-you-will-be-doing&quot; data-line=&quot;17&quot;&gt;What You Will Be Doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p id=&quot;make-quantum-opswats-crm&quot; data-line=&quot;19&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make Quantum OPSWAT&#39;s CRM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-line=&quot;21&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;previewStrong_6bbb1f98&quot;&gt;Own the system of record.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Make Quantum the place where accounts, contacts, leads, opportunities and activities are created, owned and changed, so every other system reads from it rather than the other way round.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;previewStrong_6bbb1f98&quot;&gt;Identity Quantum owns.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Build and extend the identity model: stable keys, human-readable record codes, and external IDs held as a map, so that connecting or retiring a system is a configuration change, not a migration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;previewStrong_6bbb1f98&quot;&gt;Create, edit and merge.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Build the create and edit paths for every core record, with validation at the gate, duplicate detection, and merge and alias handling so the same company or person never exists twice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;previewStrong_6bbb1f98&quot;&gt;Customization as metadata.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Build the schema registry that lets Sales Ops define custom fields, picklists, field-level security and field history without a code change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;previewStrong_6bbb1f98&quot;&gt;Keep connected systems in step.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Build a durable outbox and event stream so CPQ, ERP, marketing, the data master and AI agents receive every change reliably: retried, visible and never silently lost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;previewStrong_6bbb1f98&quot;&gt;Migrate with confidence.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Plan and run the move of data and workflows into Quantum: historical backfill, parallel runs, continuous reconciliation and staged cutover, without disrupting the sales team mid-quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p id=&quot;build-what-sales-uses-every-day&quot; data-line=&quot;28&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build what Sales uses every day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-line=&quot;30&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;previewStrong_6bbb1f98&quot;&gt;Forecasting and pipeline.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Build and evolve forecast calls, hierarchy roll-ups, deal health scoring, slip and pull-in analysis, and sales leaderboards. These are numbers leaders commit to, so they must be correct, scoped to what each viewer is allowed to see, and explainable down to the deal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;previewStrong_6bbb1f98&quot;&gt;The seller&#39;s workspace.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Build the deal grid with inline editing, the deal and account views, and the Quantum for Chrome side panel that lets a rep update a deal or log an activity from Outlook, LinkedIn or any page.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;previewStrong_6bbb1f98&quot;&gt;AI-native account research and deal intelligence.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Build research briefs that pull together account history, firmographics, intent, website visits, support cases and hiring signals into grounded, cited guidance, with ICP-fit and readiness scores that explain themselves in plain language. Choose models per task on evidence, not preference.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;previewStrong_6bbb1f98&quot;&gt;Quote to order.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Build the Order Operations review of closed-won deals: deterministic gate checks plus AI reads of purchase orders and contracts, integrated with DealHub quotes, NetSuite and fulfillment, so orders book faster with fewer round trips to Sales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;previewStrong_6bbb1f98&quot;&gt;Sales Operations center.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Build territories, seats and coverage, targets and quotas, and joiner / leaver / mover cases from BambooHR, with every change dated, approved where it needs to be, and published to every system that relies on it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p id=&quot;build-it-ai-native-and-trustworthy&quot; data-line=&quot;36&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build it AI-native and trustworthy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-line=&quot;38&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;previewStrong_6bbb1f98&quot;&gt;Agents as first-class users.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Expose Quantum&#39;s data and actions through its MCP server so OPSWAT&#39;s assistants and agents can answer &quot;what&#39;s my commit this quarter&quot;, explain a deal&#39;s health, log a meeting or propose a close-date change in natural language, with the same access rules as the UI and a preview-and-confirm step before any write.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;previewStrong_6bbb1f98&quot;&gt;Access and trust.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Extend record-level access control, roles and page access, and handle sensitive data (including compensation-adjacent data) with least privilege and a full audit trail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;previewStrong_6bbb1f98&quot;&gt;Leverage OPSWAT&#39;s agentic SDLC.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Use the Platform team&#39;s agentic coding tools as your primary means of production, own the quality and security of what ships, and document the system as you go so it stays knowable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p id=&quot;keep-quantum-running&quot; data-line=&quot;42&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep Quantum running&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-line=&quot;44&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the health of Quantum&#39;s integrations: data sync, webhooks, DealHub, NetSuite, ZoomInfo and the nightly jobs that feed forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage production incidents across Quantum and its neighbors: find the root cause, fix it permanently, and write down what happened.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship through staging to production behind feature flags, with database migrations that keep one clean chain, and verify on staging before anything reaches users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-we-need-from-you&quot; data-line=&quot;48&quot;&gt;What We Need From You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-line=&quot;50&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years building and operating production software, with at least 3 in Python backend services (FastAPI or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated, recent, daily practice building software with AI coding agents (Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot agent mode, Codex or similar). You can show us the workflow, the review and test loop, and something real that shipped through it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full-stack delivery: TypeScript and React to a working level. You can take a feature from database to screen without a hand-off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PostgreSQL to a strong level: schema design, JSONB, migrations with Alembic, row-level scoping, and query performance work you can describe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CRM and system-of-record engineering: you have built or extended a CRM&#39;s data model (accounts, contacts, opportunities, activities), its APIs and its integrations, including identity, deduplication and data migration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on integration engineering against real vendor APIs (REST, webhooks, OAuth 2.0, rate limits, retries), built and operated, not configured through a wizard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production experience with background jobs and event-driven patterns: queues, outboxes, idempotency keys, replay, and jobs that recover cleanly after a failure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping LLM features into a product: retrieval, tool calling, structured outputs, evaluation sets used to gate releases, confidence thresholds, fallbacks and guardrails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud deployment on Azure or AWS: containers, CI/CD with GitHub Actions, secrets management, observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and spoken English, and the ability to explain a technical trade-off to a sales leader or Sales Ops manager in their terms, and to push back when the data says otherwise. Vietnamese is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;it-would-be-nice-if-you-had&quot; data-line=&quot;62&quot;&gt;It Would Be Nice If You Had&lt;/h2&gt;
