&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a hands-on Senior AI Native Software Engineer to join our Enterprise Platform teams. You will build and continuously improve OPSWAT&#39;s leading cybersecurity products for protecting the world&#39;s critical infrastructure;&amp;nbsp; setting the technical bar, driving AI-augmented engineering practices, and shaping how we design, build, and ship secure software at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and ship complex, high-quality software across AI SDLC, with strong performance, scalability, and security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI-assisted tools (e.g., GitHub Copilot, Claude, Cursor) across coding, testing, refactoring, code review, and documentation and help define team standards and guardrails for responsible AI use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype, evaluate, and productionize AI/LLM (Large Language Model) capabilities within OPSWAT products where they add customer value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product managers, designers, and engineers to define requirements, design features, and deliver high-impact products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead code reviews, troubleshoot complex defects and production issues, and enforce engineering best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement of development processes, tools, and standards, including AI-augmented workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership architectural discussions, own key technical decisions, and mentor junior and mid-level developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document technical designs, specifications, and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Need from You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 05 years of relevant experience, including owning complex features or systems end to end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with both back-end (.NET, Python) and front-end (ReactJS, HTML and CSS, Tailwind, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience using AI-assisted development tools, with sound judgment on where AI adds value and where human oversight is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of data structures, algorithms, software design principles and patterns, and software development methodologies (Agile, Scrum, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with database design and technologies (SQL, NoSQL, such as MSSQL/Postgres, CosmosDB).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing, creating, and maintaining REST APIs, and proficiency with version control (e.g., Git, BitBucket).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with testing frameworks and methodologies (unit, integration, end-to-end).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving, communication, and collaboration skills, with the ability to lead initiatives independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It Would be Nice if You Had&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or integrating LLM/AI features (e.g., RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation), prompt engineering, AI agents, or AI SDKs) into production software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud platforms (e.g., Azure, AWS), CI/CD (Continuous Integration/Continuous Delivery) pipelines, and DevOps practices (e.g., TeamCity, BitBucket).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with containerization (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the cybersecurity domain or another industry relevant to OPSWAT.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
